/* Gamestage fonts, paper theme (GSUI-60).

   The paper theme names IBM Plex Sans for interface text and Instrument Serif
   for the numbers a player tracks. Neither is in the base pairing, so neither
   is on the page unless this stylesheet is, and a paper install without it
   falls through to system-ui and Georgia and reads as a recolour.

   Both faces are the paper theme's own, so the `fonts-paper` item ships them.
   It still depends on `@gamestage/fonts`, because a page using the paper theme
   still renders components that ask for the base families.

   Import once at the root, before gamestage-tokens.css. Nothing here reaches a
   third-party origin; the reason, the licences and the provenance are in
   gamestage-fonts/README.md (GSUI-149). The url() paths are relative to this
   stylesheet and resolve the same way in this repository and in a customer's
   app.

   Instrument Serif is two static files rather than one variable file, because
   the family has no weight axis: one upright, one italic, 400 each. */

@font-face {
  font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-stretch: 100%;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url('./gamestage-fonts/ibm-plex-sans-latin.woff2') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}

@font-face {
  font-family: 'Instrument Serif';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url('./gamestage-fonts/instrument-serif-latin.woff2') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}

@font-face {
  font-family: 'Instrument Serif';
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url('./gamestage-fonts/instrument-serif-italic-latin.woff2') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}
